---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { email } from '../../data/products';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy and cookies"
  description="How the RCLabs public product site stores display preferences and, when enabled and accepted, uses Google Analytics 4."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">RCLabs</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span aria-current="page">Privacy &amp; cookies</span>
      </nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY / PUBLIC PRODUCT SITE</p>
      <h1>Privacy and cookies</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        This notice explains the browser storage and optional analytics used on
        the RCLabs public product site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      RCLabs is responsible for this site. For privacy questions, email
      <!--email_off-->
      <a href={'mailto:' + email + '?subject=Privacy%20question'}>{email}</a>
      <!--/email_off-->.
    </p>

    <h2>Display preferences</h2>
    <p>
      If you choose a display setting, the site can save your text size,
      line width, spacing, and movement preference in this browser so it can
      restore them on a later visit. Open Reading &amp; display settings and
      uncheck “Save these settings in this browser” to stop saving and clear the
      saved choices. Your current choices continue to work until you leave.
    </p>

    <h2>Optional Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      On production builds where analytics is enabled, Google Analytics 4 runs
      only after you choose “Accept analytics.” Before that choice, the Google
      tag is not loaded and analytics cookies are not set. If you reject or
      withdraw, analytics stays off and the site removes the Google Analytics
      cookies it can access.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics measures page visits, the referring site’s origin, approved
      campaign tags, calls to action, and interactions with synthetic product
      samples. It uses a pseudonymous browser identifier to connect visits in
      that browser. The site does not send names, email addresses, sample-filter
      text, or the full email link to Google Analytics. A click on an email link
      is measured as a click; the site cannot tell whether you sent an email.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google Analytics also collects standard session statistics and technical
      details such as browser, device, operating system, language, screen size,
      and approximate location. Google says it uses the IP address at collection
      to derive location, then discards it before the data is logged. See
      <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/11593727">
        Google’s data collection summary
      </a>
      and
      <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/11598602">
        regional data collection details
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      The site does not use Google Analytics for advertising, remarketing,
      cross-site tracking, or cross-device identity. Google Analytics user/event
      detail is configured to expire after two months. Google may process
      analytics data under its applicable terms and privacy practices. Read
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a>
      and
      <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6366371">
        Google’s guidance on avoiding personally identifiable information
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2>Change or withdraw your choice</h2>
    <p>
      You can reopen Cookie preferences from the footer at any time. Your
      preference is kept in this browser for up to six months, then the site
      asks again. Changing your choice takes effect on the current page.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Email <!--email_off-->
      <a href={'mailto:' + email + '?subject=Privacy%20question'}>{email}</a>
      <!--/email_off--> if you have a question about this notice.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
